From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:11:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: preserve software VLAN insertion for frame taggers

Disable conduit VLAN TX features when a tagger writes into the Ethernet frame. Keep this packet-layout policy independent of flowtable block ownership.

Split from:
  0943-net-dsa-flowtable-and-vlan-transport.patch - net: dsa: coordinate flowtable forwarding and VLAN transport

Previous merged from (0943-net-dsa-flowtable-and-vlan-transport.patch):
  0943-net-dsa-offer-a-flowtable-to-the-switch-before-the-conduit.patch
  0944-net-dsa-keep-TX-VLAN-offload-off-under-a-tag-in-the-frame.patch

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/net/dsa/user.c
+++ b/net/dsa/user.c
@@ -2877,6 +2877,13 @@ void dsa_user_setup_tagger(struct net_de
 	user->hw_features |= NETIF_F_HW_TC;
 	if (user->needed_tailroom)
 		user->features &= ~(NETIF_F_SG | NETIF_F_FRAGLIST);
+	/* A tag the conduit inserts would land in front of the one written
+	 * into the frame, so the VLAN tag is pushed before it.
+	 */
+	if (cpu_dp->tag_ops->needed_headroom ||
+	    cpu_dp->tag_ops->needed_tailroom)
+		user->features &= ~(NETIF_F_HW_VLAN_CTAG_TX |
+				    NETIF_F_HW_VLAN_STAG_TX);
 	if (ds->needs_standalone_vlan_filtering)
 		user->features |= NETIF_F_HW_VLAN_CTAG_FILTER;
 
